hadiths[113]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2496","The Apostle of Allah ﷺ owed me a debt; he paid me back and made an addition (of this). I entered the mosque and he (the Holy Prophet) said to me: Observe two rak'ahs of prayer. (Using translation from Muslim 715a)"
"2497","Abu Qatadah reported the Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) as saying; when any one of you enters the mosque, he should pray two RAKAHS before sitting down. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 467)"
"2498","“When one of you enters the mosque, let him perform two Rak’ah before he sits down.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1013)"
"2499","“When one of you enters the mosque, let him perform two Rak’ah before he sits down.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1013)"
"2500","narrate: Sayyiduna Sulaik Ghatafani (may Allah be pleased with him) entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was delivering the sermon, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed him, and he performed two units of prayer. In narrating this tradition, the narrator named Hafs is unique; he was the judge of Kufa. This has been stated by the Shaykh."
"2501","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Before sitting down, perform two short rak‘ahs."
"2502","Sulaik Ghatafani came on Friday when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He (Sulaik) sat down. He (the Holy Prophet) said to him: 0 Sulaik I stand and observe two rak'ahs and make them short, and then said: When any one of you comes on Friday, while the Imam delivers the sermon, he should observe two rak'ahs and should make them short. (Using translation from Muslim 875g)"
"2503","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was present on the pulpit at that time."
"2504","Sayyiduna Sulaik Ghatafani (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the mosque on the day of Jumu'ah while the Prophet (peace and blessings of"
"2505","The Prophet (pe"
"2506","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to mix with us so much that he would say to my younger brother, ""O Abu Umair! What happened to your little bird?"" When the time for prayer came, we spread our mat for the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed prayer on it and we prayed behind him. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that ""the time for prayer had come"" means that it was the time for a voluntary (nafl) prayer. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would not perform the obligatory prayer in congregation at the house of any Ansari except in the mosque where congregational prayer was held."
"2507","The most beloved deed to him was that which a servant does regularly, even if it is little."
"2508","that she said, ""I never saw the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ pray his supererogatory prayers while sitting; until a year before his passing when he would his supererogatory prayers while sitting and reciting the sūrah in ˹such a slow˺ measured manner that it became longer than his ˹usual˺ longer ones."" (Using translation from Aḥmad 26441)"
"2509","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) became advanced in age, he used to perform voluntary prayers while sitting. When about thirty verses of a surah remained, he would stand up and recite them, then go into bowing (ruku)."
"2510","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray standing at night for a long time, and used to pray sitting at night for a long time. When he prayed standing, he bowed standing, and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 955)"
"2511","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray standing and sitting. If he started to pray standing, he would bow standing and if he started to pray sitting, he would bow sitting."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1647)"
"2512","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to perform prayer sitting on all fours."
"2513","It was narrated from ‘Imran bin Husain that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man who prays sitting down. He said, “Whoever performs prayer standing up, that is better. Whoever performs prayer sitting down will have half the reward of one who prays standing. And whoever performs prayer lying down will have half the reward of one who prays sitting.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1231)"
"2514","I asked Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would come to you, what would he do first, and when he would leave from you, what would he do? Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would enter the house, the first thing he would do was use the miswak, and when he would leave, he would perform two units of voluntary prayer."
"2515","I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying (Nafl prayer) on a donkey's back while his face was turned towards Khaibar. (Using translation from Muslim 700e)"
"2516","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand then I came back to him while he was praying. I greeted him with the salam and he gestured to me. When he finished he called me and said: 'You greeted me with Salam just now and I was praying.' And he was facing toward the east that day."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1189)"
"2517","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to perform prayer during travel on his mount, facing whatever direction it was headed."
"2518","I returned to him, he was riding (on his mount) and moving. I greeted him with salam, and he gestured to me with his blessed hand. Then I greeted him again, and he gestured again. He did not speak to me. After that, he called me and said: At that time, I was performing a voluntary prayer."
"2519","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand, then I came back to him while he was facing the east or the west. I greeted him with salam and he gestured to me. Then when he finished he called me and said: ""O Jabir!"" So I came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I greeted you with Salam but you did not answer."" He said: 'I was praying.' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1190)"
"2520","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performing prayer on his mount facing towards the east during the expedition of Anmar."
"2521","narrates: We participated in a battle along with the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and the Prophet (peace be upon him) would perform voluntary prayers on his mount, which would be facing towards the east. But when he had to perform an obligatory prayer, he would dismount and perform it facing the Qiblah."
"2522","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performing voluntary prayers on his mount during travel, and he was indicating (bowing and prostrating) with the movement of his head."
"2523","I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing prayer on his mount. He was offering voluntary prayers, regardless of which direction he was facing. However, while prostrating, he would bend lower than he did in bowing. He was performing bowing and prostration by gestures."
"2524","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performing voluntary prayers on his mount, regardless of which direction it was facing, and he was making gestures for bowing and prostration, and he would bend lower in prostration than in bowing."
"2525","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performing voluntary prayers on his mount; in prostration, he would bend lower than in bowing."
"2526","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): Did the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) use to perform prayer at the time of Duha? She replied: No, but if he returned from a journey (then on that occasion he would perform prayer at that time)."
"2527","I asked 'A'isha whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to observe the forenoon prayer. She said: No, but when he came back from the journey. (Using translation from Muslim 717a)"
"2528","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would only perform the Duha prayer when he returned from a journey. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) have negated that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed the Duha prayer. However, when he returned from a journey or after being absent from the city, (the ruling is different). His purpose was to meet the people in the mosque, not at home. The reason for this is that it was among the manners of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) that when he returned from a journey, he would first go to the mosque and perform two rak‘ahs there. So, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would often return from a journey or a battle at the time of Duha, which is the early part of the day. And the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) has prohibited that a person should go to his wife at night (after a long absence)."
"2529","“I asked ‘Aishah: ‘Did the Prophet ﷺ pray Duha?’ She said: ‘Yes; four (Rak’ah) and he would add whatever Allah willed.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1381)"
"2530","I never saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performing voluntary prayers (nawafil) while sitting, until one year before his passing, I saw him performing voluntary prayers while sitting. He would recite the Surah slowly and with pauses, to the extent that it seemed even longer than the Surah itself."
"2531","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came to me and he performed eight rak'ahs of Duha (forenoon) prayer."
"2532","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) did not perform the Duha prayer. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to perform this prayer. She stated that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) left many actions out of fear that people might adopt them as Sunnah and then they might become obligatory upon them."
"2533","Messenger of Allah narrated that Allah, Blessed and Most High said: ""Son of Adam: Perform four Rak'ah for Me in the beginning of the day it will suffice you for the latter part of it."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 475)"
"2534","I will suffice you in its latter part.”"
"2535","I have never seen any expedition return so quickly and receive as much booty as this expedition has received. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of something by which you can return even more quickly and obtain even more spoils? A person performs ablution well at home, then goes to the mosque and offers the morning prayer, then (remains seated there and then) offers the forenoon (Duha) prayer; such a person returns quickly and obtains even more spoils."
"2536","""My dearest friend advised me (to do) three things: 'To sleep after praying Witr, to fast three days each month, and to pray two rak'ahs of Fajr.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1677)"
"2537","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Umm Hani, whoever you have given protection to, we also give protection to him. Sayyidah Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) poured water and performed ghusl (ritual bath), then wrapped a cloth as a sheet and placed its ends on the opposite sides (of his shoulders), then he offered eight rak‘ahs at the time of Duha (forenoon)."
"2538","I investigated this matter and was very eager to find someone who could inform me about it—whether the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed the Duha prayer. I found only Lady Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her), who informed me about this: She told me that on the day of the conquest of Makkah, after the day had advanced, the Prophet (peace be upon him) arrived. By his order, a cloth was hung for his privacy, and he performed ghusl (ritual bath). Then he stood up and performed eight rak‘ahs. I cannot determine whether his standing, his bowing, or his prostration was longer; all of these were nearly equal in length. Lady Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) states: I never saw him perform voluntary prayers at that time, either before or after this occasion."
"2539","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""The prayer of the righteous is at the time when the sand becomes hot for the (camel) calves."
"2540","The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied: ""Remove something harmful from the path, or else perform two rak'ahs at the time of Duha (forenoon)."
"2541","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and saw that the people were praying during (the night of) Ramadan in the corner of the mosque. He asked: Who are these people ? It was said to him that those were people who had not learnt Quran. But Ubayy b. Ka'b is praying and they would pray behind him. The Prophet ﷺ said: They did right and it is good what they did. Abu Dawud said: This tradition is not strong, the narrator Muslim b. Khalid is weak. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1377)"
"2542","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in the masjid one night, and some people followed his prayer. Then he prayed the following night and more people came. Then they gathered on the third or fourth night and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out to them. When morning came he said: ""I saw what you did, and nothing prevented me from coming out to you but the fact that I feared that this would be made obligatory for you,"" and that was in Ramadan. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1604)"
"2543","I feared that the night prayer would be made obligatory upon you and you would not be able to perform it."" (Lady Aisha narrates) The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to encourage people to perform voluntary prayers in Ramadan. He did not command them with firmness. He used to say: ""Whoever stands (in prayer) in the Night of Decree (Laylat al-Qadr) with faith and seeking reward, Allah will forgive his past sins."" The narrator states: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away, this matter remained as it was. During the caliphate of Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) and in the early period of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), the matter remained the same until Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) gathered the people behind Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), and he used to lead them in Tarawih in Ramadan. This was the first gathering of people behind a reciter in Ramadan."
"2544","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out during the night and observed prayer in the mosque and some of the people prayed along with him. When it was morning the people talked about this and so a large number of people gathered there. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the second night, and they (the people) prayed along with him. When it was morning the people began to talk about it. So the mosque thronged with people on the third night. He (the Holy Prophet) came out and they prayed along with him. When it was the fourth night, the mosque was filled to its utmost capacity but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out. Some persons among then cried:"" Prayer."" But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come to them till he came out for the morning prayer. When he had completed the morning prayer, he turned his face to the people and recited Tashahhud (I bear testi- mony that there is no god but Allah and I bear testimony that Muhammad is His Messen- ger) and then said: Your affair was not hidden from me in the night, but I was afraid that (my observing prayer continuously) might make the night prayer obligatory for you and you might be unable to perform it. (Using translation from Muslim 761b)"
"2545","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out during the night and observed prayer in the mosque and some of the people prayed along with him. When it was morning the people talked about this and so a large number of people gathered there. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the second night, and they (the people) prayed along with him. When it was morning the people began to talk about it. So the mosque thronged with people on the third night. He (the Holy Prophet) came out and they prayed along with him. When it was the fourth night, the mosque was filled to its utmost capacity but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out. Some persons among then cried:"" Prayer."" But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come to them till he came out for the morning prayer. When he had completed the morning prayer, he turned his face to the people and recited Tashahhud (I bear testi- mony that there is no god but Allah and I bear testimony that Muhammad is His Messen- ger) and then said: Your affair was not hidden from me in the night, but I was afraid that (my observing prayer continuously) might make the night prayer obligatory for you and you might be unable to perform it. (Using translation from Muslim 761b)"
"2546","""I heard the Messenger of Allah say concerning Ramadan: 'Whoever spends its night in prayer (Qiyam) out of faith and in the hope of reward, he will be forgiven his previous sins.""' ' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2194)"
"2547","""We fasted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Ramadan and he did not lead us in praying Qiyam until there were seven days left in the month, when he led us in praying Qiyam until one-third of the night had passed. Then he did not lead us in praying Qiyam when there were six days left. Then he led us praying Qiyam when there were five days left until one-half of the night had passed. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What if we spend the rest of this night praying Nafl?"" He said: ""Whoever prays Qiyam with the Imam until he finishes, Allah (SWT) will record for him the Qiyam of a (whole) night."" Then he did not lead us in prayer or pray Qiyam until there were three days of the month left. Then he led us in praying Qiyam when there were three days left. He gathered his family and wives (and led us in prayer) until we feared that we would miss Al-Falah. I (one of the narrators) said: ""What is Al-Falah?"" He said: ""The suhur"". (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1605)"
"2548","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, rather twenty-two (22) days have passed and seven days remain; sometimes the month is of twenty-nine (29) days, so seek this night."
"2549","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: What was it, O Ubayy? He said: There were some women in our house. They said: We cannot recite the Qur'an, so we follow your prayer. The narrator says: I led them in eight rak'ahs and then I performed witr. (Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) seemed to express approval; he did not say anything to him: No."
"2550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: O Ubayy! What was it? He replied: The women of my household said: We cannot recite the Qur'an, so we will follow your prayer. Sayyiduna Ubayy said: I led those women in eight rak'ahs of prayer, then I performed witr. (Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates) So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) seemed to express approval, however, he said something to him: No."
"2551","He presented himself before Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: Tell me about the character of the Prophet (peace be upon"
"2552","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed any prayer, he liked to perform it regularly. And if, due to sleep or illness or any other engagement such as difficulty, he was unable to perform the night voluntary prayers, then he would perform twelve rak’ahs during the day."
"2553","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: When one you sleeps, the devil ties three knots at the back of his neck, sealing every knot with, ""You have a long night, so sleep."" So if one awakes and mentions Allah, a knot will be loosened; if he performs ablution another knot will be loosened; and if he prays, the third knot will be loosened; and in the morning he will be active and in good spirits; otherwise he will be in bad spirits and sluggish. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1306)"
"2554","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: Whenever any man or woman (goes to sleep), a knot is tied on their head at the time of sleeping. If they wake up and remember Allah Almighty, the knot is untied. If they get up, perform ablution, and offer prayer, then all the knots are untied."
"2555","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amr رضي الله عنه narrates: I have never reported anything regarding the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم except what the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم himself said. I heard the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم say: \""Whoever deliberately attributes a lie to me should prepare his abode in Hell.\"" And I heard the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم say: \""A person from my Ummah gets up at night, he goes to perform ablution, and there are knots upon him. When he washes his hands, one knot is untied; when he was"
"2556","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whenever a Muslim man or woman sleeps, knots are tied upon him. When he wakes up and remembers Allah, one knot is untied. If he performs ablution and stands for prayer, he wakes up energetic, having attained goodness, and all his knots are untied. But if he wakes up and does not remember Allah, he wakes up with all his knots still tied, and he wakes up with a heavy mind in a state of laziness, and he does not attain goodness."
"2557","The second person is the one who participates in jihad in the way of Allah. People retreat, but this person also knows what calamity will befall him if he retreats, and what reward he will receive if he returns (to the battlefield), so he returns (to the battlefield) until his blood is shed. Then Allah Almighty says to His angels: Look at My servant, he returned hoping for what is with Me and fearing what is with Me, until his blood was shed.”"
"2558","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Our Lord is pleased with two men: one who gets up from his bed and blanket, leaving his wife, and goes towards prayer. Allah Almighty says to His angels: Look at My servant who has risen from his bed and from his wife to come towards prayer, desiring what is with Me and fearing what is with Me. And the second is the person who participates in jihad in the way of Allah; his companions retreat, but he knows what punishment there is for retreating and what reward there is for returning (to the battle), so he returns until his blood is shed. Allah Almighty says to the angels: Look at My servant, he returned hoping for what is with Me and fearing what is with Me, until his blood was shed.”"
"2559","The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Everything was created from water."" I said, ""Tell me about something, if I act upon it, I will enter Paradise."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Feed others, spread the greeting of peace, maintain the ties of kinship, and pray at night when people are sleeping; you will enter Paradise in peace."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, ""Tell me about everything,"" means he intended to ask about everything that was created from water. And the evidence for this being correct is the answer given by the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Everything was created from water."" So this answer was given exactly in accordance with the question. It does not mean that everything was created from water, even if it is not a created being."
"2560","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""That which he recites will soon prevent him from that deed."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The words of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""That which he recites will soon prevent him,"" are of the type about which we have written in our books that sometimes the Arabs attribute an action to the action itself just as they attribute it to the doer. So the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intent is that when the prayer is genuine in its beginning and end, then the one who prays, along with his prayer, refrains from prohibited things. Its example is the saying of Allah Almighty: ""Indeed, prayer prevents indecency and wrongdoing."
"2561","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There is an hour during the night in which, if any Muslim servant asks Allah Almighty for any good of this world or the Hereafter, Allah Almighty will grant it to him."
"2562","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Satan has urinated in his ear."" (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) ""in both his ears?"" The narrator named Sufyan says: In our view, what is meant by this is the person who remains asleep at the time of the obligatory prayer."
"2563","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: After the obligatory prayers, which prayer is the most virtuous? The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The prayer performed in the middle of the night. He was asked: After the month of Ramadan, which fast is the most virtuous? The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The fast of Allah’s month which people call Muharram."
"2564","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) which night prayer is the best, so Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the same question that you have asked me, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""At the middle of the night, or perhaps in the middle part of the night."" This doubt is from ‘Awf."
"2565","“Whoever among you fears that he will not wake up at the end of the night, let him pray Witr at the beginning of the night, then go to sleep. Whoever hopes that he will wake up at the end of the night, let him pray Witr at the end of the night, for recitation (of the Qur’an) at the end of the night is attended (by the angels), and that is better.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1187)"
"2566","O Messenger of Allah, our souls are in the hand of Allah and if He wills to wake us up, He will wake us up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left when I said that to him and I heard him, as he was leaving, strike his hand against his thigh and say: ʿBut, man is ever more quarrelsome than anythingʿ (al-Kahf:18:54). (Using translation from Aḥmad 575)"
"2567","The Prophet ﷺ said: May Allah have mercy on a man who gets up at night and prays, and awakens his wife; if she refuses, he should sprinkle water on her face. May Allah have mercy on a woman who gets up at night and prays, and awakens her husband; if he refuses, she would sprinkle water on his face. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1308)"
"2568","The Prophet ﷺ said: When a man himself wakes at night and wakens his wife and they pray two rak'ahs together, they are recorded among the men and women who make much mention of Allah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1451)"
"2569","‘When a man wakes up at night and wakes his wife, and they pray two Rak’ah, they will be recorded among the men and women who remember Allah much.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1335)"
"2570","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), he wrapped his Hadrami cloak as a mantle at night and performed voluntary prayers; there was nothing else on his body besides it."
"2571","The Prophet ﷺ used to construct a loom with a Hasir at night m order to pray therein, and during the day he used to spread it out and sit on it. The people started coming to the Prophet ﷺ at night to offer the prayer behind him When their number increased, the Prophet ﷺ faced them and said. O people! Do only those good deeds which you can do, for Allah does not get tired (of giving reward) till you get tired, and the best deeds to Allah are the incessant ones though they were few. (Using translation from Bukhārī 5861)"
"2572","The narrator named Abu Suwaid is Hamid bin Suwaid, and he is from Egypt. The person who mentioned his name as Abu Suwayyah was mistaken."
"2573","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A qintar consists of twelve thousand uqiyyah, and each uqiyyah among them is better than everything that exists in the heavens and the earth."
"2574","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever recites Surah Yasin at night seeking the pleasure of Allah Almighty, his sins will be forgiven."
"2575","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""If somebody recited the last two Verses of Surat Al-Baqara at night, that will be sufficient for him."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5009)"
"2576","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Reciting Surah Ikhlas is equal to reciting one third of the Qur'an."
"2577","narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: ""This journey is a cause of hardship and burden, so when a person performs Witr, he should also perform two rak'ahs. If he wakes up (at the time of Fajr prayer), then fine, otherwise these two will suffice for him."
"2578","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition force [comprised] of many, and he asked each what he could recite, so each one of them mentioned what he could recite - meaning what he had memorized of the Qur'an. He came to one of the youngest men among them and said: 'What have you memorized O so-and-so?' He said: 'I memorized this and that and Surat Al-Baqarah.' He said: 'You memorized Surat Al-Baqarah?' He said: ""Yes.' He said: ""Then go, for you are their commander.' A man among their chief said: 'By Allah [O Messenger of Allah]! Nothing prevented me from learning Surat Al-Baqarah except fearing that I would not be able to stand with (in voluntary night prayer).' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Learn the Qur'an to recite it, for indeed the parable of the Qur'an for the one who recites it and stands with it (in prayer) is that of a bag full of musk whose scent fills the air all around. And the parable of the one who learns it then sleeps while it is in his memory is that of a bag containing musk that is tied shut.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2876)"
"2579","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) slept until half the night had passed. It was either a little before or after half the night when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) woke up. He wiped his hands over his face to remove the effects of sleep, then he recited the last ten verses of Surah Al-Imran. After that, he went towards a hanging water-skin and performed ablution from it."
"2580","narrates: (Sometimes) the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would begin to offer voluntary prayers while sitting. He would recite the surah with pauses, reciting it slowly, until it would seem longer than a surah that was actually longer than it."
"2581","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would be reciting (Qur'an) in his chamber, and a person outside the chamber could hear it."
"2582","I asked Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): What do you say about the Prophet (peace be upon him)? Did he recite aloud or in a low voice while praying? Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: Sometimes he would recite aloud and sometimes in a low voice. So I said: All praise is due to Allah, who has provided flexibility in this matter."
"2583","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""When a person feels sleepy at the time of prayer, he should go to sleep until his sleep is over, because it may happen that a person stands for prayer while he is drowsy and, thinking he is supplicating for forgiveness, he may actually be cursing himself."
"2584","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If a man feels drowsy when he is praying, let him stop, lest he supplicate against himself without realizing.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 162)"
"2585","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: When one of you gets up by night (to pray), and falters in reciting the Qur'an (due to sleep), and he does not understand what he utters, he should sleep. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1311)"
"2586","I said, ""This is Hawla bint Tuwait. People say that she does not sleep at night."" Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""She does not sleep at night? You people should do as much (good) deeds as you have the strength for. By Allah! Allah’s bounty does not cease until you yourselves become weary."
"2587","The people replied: ""So-and-so woman performs prayer, and when she fears sleep overcoming her, she holds onto it."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""She should pray as long as she is alert, and when sleep overcomes her, she should go to sleep."
"2588","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr Ghifari (may Allah be pleased with him) (the narrator is in doubt) or perhaps Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him)—this doubt is from the narrator named Shu’bah—he stated that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Whoever intends in his mind to perform voluntary prayers during a part of the night, but he remains asleep at that time, then that sleep is a charity from Allah Almighty upon him, and that person receives the reward according to his intention.”"
"2589","""I came to Al-Aswad bin Yazid, who was a close friend of mine and said: 'O Abu 'Amr, tell me what the Mother of the Believers told you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'She said: ""He used to sleep for the first part of the night and stay up for the latter part.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1640)"
"2590","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, ""The most beloved fasting to Allah was the fasting of (the Prophet) David who used to fast on alternate days. And the most beloved prayer to Allah was the prayer of David who used to sleep for (the first) half of the night and pray for 1/3 of it and (again) sleep for a sixth of it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3420)"
"2591","When the Prophet ﷺ got up to pray at night, he would brush his teeth with the siwak. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1621)"
"2592","That he spent a night with Maimunah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who was also his (Ibn 'Abbas's) maternal aunt. I lay towards the width of the pillow and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his wife slept towards its length. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept. When half the night passed, or a little before it or a little after it, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ awoke and began to rub his face (eyes) to remove the sleep. He then recited ten verses from the last part of Surah 'Al-Imran. Hen then came to a bag of water that was hanging. He performed ablution from it and performed his ablution well. He then stood up and prayed. I also got up and did as he did. I then went and stood at his side. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his right hand upon my head and took me by my ear twisting it. He then prayed two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs. The narrator al-Qa'nabi said: Six times. He observed the witr prayer, and then slept until the mu'adhdhin came. He got up and prayed two light rak'ahs and then came out and offered the dawn prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1367)"
"2593","narrator has clarified some words)"
"2594","The Prophet (peace be upon him) kept reciting during his night prayers: “Glory is to my Lord, and praise is for Him; glory is to my Lord, praise is for Him.” He continued reciting this for quite a while. Then he kept reciting: “Glory is to the Lord of all the worlds, and glory is to the Lord of all the worlds.” He continued reciting this for quite a while."
"2595","""I used to stay overnight at the Prophet's ﷺ apartment and I used to hear him when he prayed Qiyam at night saying: 'Subhan Allahi Rabil-Alamin (Glory be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds)' for a long time, then he said: 'Subhan Allah wa bi hamdih (Glory and praise be to Allah) for a long time."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1618)"
"2596","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever wakes up in the morning and says upon waking: La ilaha illallah wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu, wa Huwa ‘ala kulli shay’in Qadir; Subhan-Allah walhamdu lillahi, wa la ilaha illallahu, wa Allahu Akbar, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa billahil-‘Aliyil-‘Azim (None has the right to be worshipped but Allah alone, with no partner or associate. His is the dominion and all praise is to Him, and He is Able to do all things. Glory is to Allah, praise is to Allah, none has the right to be worshiped but Allah, Allah is the Most Great, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah, the Most High, the Most Supreme), then he supplicates Rabbighfirli (O Lord, forgive me), he will be forgiven.’” Walid said: “Or he said: then if he supplicated, it will be answered for him then if he stood up and performed ablution and then performed prayer, his prayer would be accepted.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3878)"
"2597","“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Tahajjud at night, he would say: “Allahumma lakal-hamd, Anta nurus-samawati wal-ard wa man fihinna. Wa lakal-hamd, Anta qayyamus-samawati wal-ard wa man fihinna. Wa lakal-hamd, Anta malikus- samawati wal-ard wa man fihinna. Wa lakal-hamd, Antal-haqq, wa waʿduka haqq, wa liqa’uka haqq, wa qawluka haqq, wal-jannatu haqq, wan-naru haqq, was-saʿatu haqq, wan-nabiyyuna haqq, wa Muhammadun haqq. Allahumma laka aslamtu, wa bika amantu, wa ʿalaika tawakkaltu wa ilaika anabtu, wa bika khasamtu, wa ilaika hakamtu, faghfirli ma qaddamtu wa ma akhkhartu, wa ma asrartu wa ma aʿlantu. Antal-muqaddimu wa Antal-muakhkhiru. La ilaha illa anta wa la ilaha ghairuka, wa la hawla wa la quwwata illa bika (O Allah, to you is praise, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth, and everyone therein. To You is praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth, and everyone therein. To You is praise, You are the Sovereign of the heavens and the earth, and everyone therein. To You is praise, You are the Truth; Your promise is true, the meeting with You is true, Your saying is true, Paradise is true, the Fire is true, the Hour is true, the Prophets are true, and Muhammad ﷺ is true. O Allah, to You have I submitted, in You I believe, in You have I put my trust, to You I turn in repentance, by Your help I argue, to You I refer my case, so forgive me for my past and future sins, what I have done in secret and what I have done openly. You are the One Who brings forward and puts back. None has the right to be worshipped but You, and there is none who has the right to be worshipped other than You. And there is no power and no strength except with You.” Another chain that Ibn ʿAbbas narrated: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood during the night for Tahajjud,” and he mentioned something similar. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1355)"
"2598","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up for praying at midnight, he said: o Allah, be praise to Thee, Thou art the light of the heavens and the earth; and to Thee be praise; Thou are the maintainer of the heavens and the earth; and to Thee be praise, Thou art the heavens and the earth and what is between them; Thou art the truth, and Thy statement is truth; and Thy promise is the truth; and the visitation with Thee is true; and the Paradise is true and the Hell-fire is true and the Hour is true; O Allah, to Thee I turned my attention, and by Thee I disputed, and to Thee I brought forth my case, so forgive me my former and latter sins, and my secret and open sins, Thou art my deity, there is no deity but Thou. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 771)"
"2599","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up for praying at midnight, he said: o Allah, be praise to Thee, Thou art the light of the heavens and the earth; and to Thee be praise; Thou are the maintainer of the heavens and the earth; and to Thee be praise, Thou art the heavens and the earth and what is between them; Thou art the truth, and Thy statement is truth; and Thy promise is the truth; and the visitation with Thee is true; and the Paradise is true and the Hell-fire is true and the Hour is true; O Allah, to Thee I turned my attention, and by Thee I disputed, and to Thee I brought forth my case, so forgive me my former and latter sins, and my secret and open sins, Thou art my deity, there is no deity but Thou. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 771)"
"2601","I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began the prayer, he recited: “Allah is the Greatest, He is the Greatest. Allah is the Greatest, He is the Greatest. Allah is the Greatest, He is the Greatest. All praise is exclusively for Allah, as much as may be. I declare the purity of Allah from every defect morning and evening. I declare the purity of Allah from every defect morning and evening. O Allah! I seek refuge with You from the devil, from his ‘hamz’, from his ‘nafth’, and from his ‘nafkh’.” The narrator named Amr says: By ‘hamz’ is meant epilepsy, by ‘nafkh’ is meant arrogance, and by ‘nafth’ is meant poetry."
"2602","""I asked 'Aishah with what did he- meaning the Prophet ﷺ- start Qiyam Al-Lail? She said: 'You have asked me something which no one before you has asked. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the takbir ten times, the tahmid ten times, the tasbih ten times, and the tahlil ten times, and pray for forgiveness ten times, and say: Allahummaghfirli, wahdini, warzuqni wa 'afini. A'udhu billahi min diqil-maqami yawmal-qiyamah (O Allah, forgive me, guide me, grant me provision and good health. I seek refuge with Allah from the difficulty of standing on the Day of Resurrection.)"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1617)"
"2603","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that when he performed voluntary prayers at night, he would raise his voice somewhat. He mentioned that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to do the same."
"2604","I performed prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whenever he recited a verse mentioning mercy, he would pause and ask for that mercy, and whenever he recited a verse mentioning punishment, he would pause and seek refuge from it."
"2605","I performed prayer one night behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and whenever he reached a verse mentioning mercy, he would pause there and ask for that mercy, and whenever he recited a verse mentioning punishment, he would pause there and seek refuge from that punishment."
"2606","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: When one of you gets up at night, he should begin the prayer with two short rak'ahs. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1323)"
"2607","I think, in the narration, these words are also present: ""He has not destroyed us because of our sins."" One of those present requested: Last night I recited all the Mufassal verses. Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This is like reciting poetry quickly. I remember those surahs that are close to each other, which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite. They are eighteen surahs from the Mufassal surahs and two surahs from the Ha-Meem group."
"2608","I shall watch the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night. I slept at the threshold of his door or of his tent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two light rak'ahs, and then prayed two long, long, long rak'ahs. He then prayed two rak'ahs that were not so long as the two rak'ahs before them ; he then prayed two rak'ahs that were less in duration, than the rak'ahs before them; again he prayed two rak'ahs that were less in length then the preceding rak'ahs; he then prayed two rak'ahs that were less in length than the previous rak'ahs. This made altogether thirteen rak'ahs. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1366)"
"2609","""I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night. He started reciting Surat Al-Baqarah and he recited one hundred verses, then did not bow, rather he continued. I thought: 'He will complete it in two rak'ahs, but he continued.' I thought: 'He will complete it and then bow,' but he continued until he recited Surat An-Nisa', then Al Imran. Then he bowed for almost as long as he had stood, saying while bowing: 'Subhan Rabbial-azim, Subhan Rabbial-azim, Subhan Rabbial-azim ( Glory be to my Lord Almighty, Glory be to my Lord Almighty, Glory be to my Lord Almighty).' Then he raised his head and said: 'Sami Allahu liman hamidah (Allah hears the one who praises Him). Then he prostrated and made his prostration lengthy, saying: ""Subhan Rabbial-A'la, Subhan Rabbial-A'la, Subhan Rabbial-A'la (Glory be to my Lord Most High, Glory be to my Lord Most High, Glory be to my Lord Most High). And he did not come to any verse that spoke of fear or glorifying Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, but he said something appropriate."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1133)"
